    public static let balance = RuleSource(level: 3, citation: "Ngo, Teo & Byrne 2003, Information Sciences 152:25-46 (abstract opened): balance, equilibrium, symmetry among 14 aesthetic measures; Bauerly & Liu 2006, IJHCS 64 (abstract opened): viewers judge balance and symmetry, symmetric layouts preferred; Arnheim, Art and Visual Perception (not opened)", note: "Weight = distance of each 16 px cell from the page background colour (0-1), a saliency-lite proxy. Four tests: centroid within 30% of centre horizontally (30) and 40% vertically (20), left/right weight ratio 0.5 or more (25), mirror similarity 0.8 or more (25). Cut-offs calibrated on the 40-site LabintheWild train split; held-out rho 0.16 (not significant). Level 3: direction supported, cut-offs own choice.")
    public static let grouping = RuleSource(level: 3, citation: "Grouping cues weighed: proximity 35, similarity 20, meaning 20, common region 15 (bonus only, never a flaw when absent), alignment 10 (minor; Wagemans et al. 2012). Wertheimer 1923 (proximity, similarity; via Wagemans et al. 2012, Psychological Bulletin 138:1172-1217, full text opened); Palmer 1992, Cognitive Psychology 24:436-447 (common region; record opened, full text not opened, cited through Wagemans 2012 s3.2.3); Kubovy, Holcombe & Wagemans 1998 (proximity: ratio of longer to shorter distance above about 1.5 and the longer grouping is almost never seen; via Wagemans 2012); Elder & Goldberg 2002 (proximity cuts grouping uncertainty about 75%, similarity and continuation about 10% each; via Wagemans 2012); Ware, Information Visualization, stage 2 pattern grouping; Ngo, Teo & Byrne 2003, Information Sciences 152:25-46 (record opened, abstract not available; their 14 measures include alignment and grouping-related order, taken from citing summaries)", note: "From OCR boxes and pixels. Boxes are linked by single-linkage on edge-to-edge gaps; a gap of 1.5x the typical gap or more splits groups (Kubovy 1998 ratio). g_align is measured inside each group only (boxes sharing a left, right or centre line with a groupmate, 60%+ of them; button text is not judged), so a centred title above left-aligned fields does not fail. Checks: proximity (35): 2 to 24 groups (more than that is a crowd of fragments, not groups; the cap of 24 is own choice, set on the Arngren test shot), 60%+ of boxes sit in a group of 2+, under 25% of gaps are ambiguous (1.2-1.5x), between-group gap is 1.5x the within-group gap or more. Alignment (25): the fixed logic from 8f3d105, 50%+ of boxes on a shared line of 3+, top 3 lines hold 35%+. Common region (20): when 15%+ of text sits on a non-page background, 75%+ of groups share one background; not applicable otherwise. Similarity (20): 60%+ of boxes in a group match its dominant size (within 25%), weight and colour. Weights are own choice, in proportion to Elder & Goldberg's cue strengths. Thresholds set by eye on the 6 test screens: the LabintheWild 40-site train split gave no usable signal (best train rho 0.15, held-out negative), so no cut-off is validated against people. Alignment moved in from the old Alignment meter; h_groups (Hierarchy) and E3 (Ease) were duplicate gap checks and are removed.")
    public static let firstImpressionValidated = "First impression is rated by Claude Sonnet from the screenshot (1-9, median of 3). Validated against real people: LabintheWild ratings (Reinecke & Gajos 2014, 418 sites; CC BY-NC-SA), 60 sites, Spearman rho 0.82 [0.68, 0.90] on all 60, 0.86 on 20 held-out sites. Score = min(100, (median-1)/7*100), so a median of 8 gives 100 (Sonnet rarely gives 9). The mapping is monotonic, so Spearman rho is unchanged. The older checklist (held-out rho 0.38) is only a fallback."
    public static let firstImpressionFit = "First impression weights (simple 30, dated 60, overlay 10) fitted on 40 of 60 LabintheWild sites (Reinecke & Gajos 2014, CC BY-NC-SA); held-out 20 sites rho 0.38. Own choice, low confidence."
